258
00:16:05,839 --> 00:16:08,258
Now we can play Oh Seong-sik's tape, too.

259
00:16:08,342 --> 00:16:09,635
That's right.

260
00:16:09,718 --> 00:16:12,805
After we found that tape,
we didn't have anywhere to play it.

261
00:16:12,888 --> 00:16:15,683
Then I thought of you, driver.

262
00:16:16,642 --> 00:16:18,727
I'm glad you remembered
and came back.

263
00:16:20,771 --> 00:16:23,607
Do you still see Pako often these days?

264
00:16:24,858 --> 00:16:27,987
Well, Pako and I...

265
00:16:28,821 --> 00:16:31,115
We went to different colleges,

266
00:16:31,198 --> 00:16:33,033
but we saw each other more
than our college friends.

267
00:16:33,659 --> 00:16:37,329
Even after we started working,
we'd see each other almost every week.

268
00:16:38,789 --> 00:16:40,124
But then...

269
00:16:40,958 --> 00:16:43,335
Pako got married and had kids,

270
00:16:43,419 --> 00:16:45,713
and it got hard to stay in touch.

271
00:16:46,422 --> 00:16:49,174
I felt awkward asking him out for drinks
on the weekend,

272
00:16:50,551 --> 00:16:52,761
when he probably barely had time
for his family as it was.

273
00:16:52,845 --> 00:16:54,430
I didn't want to impose.

274
00:16:55,139 --> 00:16:56,557
So...

275
00:16:57,391 --> 00:17:00,686
I'd send him a digital gift card
for his birthday,

276
00:17:01,353 --> 00:17:02,980
and check in on him.

277
00:17:10,404 --> 00:17:12,072
We're here!

278
00:17:12,156 --> 00:17:13,532
- Thanks for all your help.
- Sure.

279
00:17:13,615 --> 00:17:14,816
All right.

280
00:17:25,294 --> 00:17:27,629
I'd help you move your things,

281
00:17:27,713 --> 00:17:28,964
but there's nothing to move.

282
00:17:29,048 --> 00:17:31,133
You already helped me move
all the way here.

283
00:17:31,216 --> 00:17:32,760
Oh, right.

284
00:17:32,843 --> 00:17:34,636
Anyway, congratulations on the move.

285
00:17:35,429 --> 00:17:36,513
Thank you.

286
00:17:48,150 --> 00:17:49,151
Why...

287
00:17:50,360 --> 00:17:54,782
- Here.
- Oh, that's right.

288
00:17:54,865 --> 00:17:58,243
Why don't you get in touch with Pako?
It's been a while.

289
00:17:58,327 --> 00:18:00,829
I'm sure he'd be happy.
I know I was.

290
00:18:01,413 --> 00:18:03,582
- I'll get going.
- All right. Take care.

291
00:19:05,769 --> 00:19:06,603
Hello?

292
00:19:07,396 --> 00:19:09,022
Hey, Pako!

293
00:19:09,857 --> 00:19:12,192
Oh, Geobang! Long time no see.

294
00:19:12,276 --> 00:19:13,277
What brings you around?

295
00:19:14,111 --> 00:19:15,154
Just felt like calling, man.

296
00:19:15,237 --> 00:19:18,240
Do I need a reason
to call you, man?

297
00:19:19,867 --> 00:19:20,742
I guess not. Sorry.

298
00:19:21,326 --> 00:19:23,745
What are you talking about?
You have nothing to apologize for.

299
00:19:23,829 --> 00:19:26,248
Hey, how are the kids doing?

300
00:19:27,499 --> 00:19:28,375
Yeah.

301
00:19:28,458 --> 00:19:30,502
The older one's grown up
a bit and calmed down,

302
00:19:31,170 --> 00:19:32,921
but the younger one smashed
my laptop yesterday.

303
00:19:33,505 --> 00:19:35,966
You have a second kid?

304
00:19:36,550 --> 00:19:39,094
Yeah, man. Two are better than one, right?

305
00:19:39,178 --> 00:19:42,389
Oh, really?

306
00:19:45,684 --> 00:19:49,146
Is your wife still really into
cross-stitching?

307
00:19:51,481 --> 00:19:53,942
Come on, that was ages ago.
You're still doing cross-stitch?

308
00:19:56,987 --> 00:19:58,947
I was just saying, man.

309
00:20:02,910 --> 00:20:04,494
Hey, what about that thing...

310
00:20:04,578 --> 00:20:08,290
You're taking your arginine
and maca, right?

311
00:20:08,957 --> 00:20:12,336
You can skip the omega-3,
but you absolutely have to take those.

312
00:20:13,462 --> 00:20:14,880
I am.

313
00:20:16,173 --> 00:20:18,842
Hey, I can't take omega-3.
It tastes too fishy.

314
00:20:19,801 --> 00:20:21,678
Hey, you can get omega-3
that doesn't taste fishy.

315
00:20:21,762 --> 00:20:23,222
Want me to send you a link?

316
00:20:23,305 --> 00:20:24,765
Yeah, send it. I'll send it to you.

317
00:20:25,432 --> 00:20:26,266
Okay.

318
00:20:28,268 --> 00:20:30,520
Hey, it's been a long time
since we saw each other, huh?

319
00:20:30,604 --> 00:20:32,397
We keep saying, 'Let's meet up,'
but never do.

320
00:20:33,899 --> 00:20:35,359
Yeah, you're right.

321
00:20:36,026 --> 00:20:38,779
Yeah, well...
Let's make time to meet sometime.

322
00:20:39,363 --> 00:20:40,864
Yeah, let's really get together soon.

323
00:20:40,948 --> 00:20:41,782
Sure.

324
00:20:42,658 --> 00:20:43,742
Get some rest.

325
00:20:43,825 --> 00:20:46,036
You too. Get some rest. I'll call you.

326
00:20:46,119 --> 00:20:47,788
Okay, take care.

327
00:20:47,871 --> 00:20:49,138
Yeah.

328
00:21:17,484 --> 00:21:18,318
Who was that?

329
00:21:19,611 --> 00:21:20,612
Seok-ju.

330
00:21:22,739 --> 00:21:23,573
Who?

331
00:21:24,157 --> 00:21:24,992
Geobang.

332
00:21:25,075 --> 00:21:26,285
Oh!

333
00:21:26,994 --> 00:21:28,370
What has he been up to lately?

334
00:21:30,914 --> 00:21:32,833
You know, a little bit of everything.

335
00:21:33,959 --> 00:21:35,419
Do you think he still hates me?

336
00:21:35,502 --> 00:21:37,462
Come on, he doesn't hate you.

337
00:21:38,046 --> 00:21:40,924
He was just on edge
when we were rehearsing the dance.

338
00:21:42,759 --> 00:21:45,137
Besides, Geobang only ever drank Milkis.

339
00:21:45,220 --> 00:21:46,722
But you, So-yeon,
kept bringing Ambasa.

340
00:21:46,805 --> 00:21:48,056
It got on his nerves, that's all.

341
00:21:49,808 --> 00:21:52,936
I bought it for you,
not for Geobang.

342
00:21:53,979 --> 00:21:56,857
Still, we were a team.
You should've shared.

343
00:21:56,940 --> 00:22:00,193
You two sound like you were on
'Gayo Top 10' or something.

344
00:22:04,531 --> 00:22:05,407
Are the kids asleep?

345
00:22:10,203 --> 00:22:12,456
I've got everything connected right...

346
00:22:12,539 --> 00:22:18,045
Why the hell isn't this working?

347
00:22:19,296 --> 00:22:21,052
Shit, I'm screwed.

348
00:22:29,014 --> 00:22:32,517
♪ Who am I, and where am I? ♪

349
00:22:32,601 --> 00:22:36,480
♪ Someone's calling me
from far away... ♪

350
00:22:36,563 --> 00:22:37,773
What's going on?

351
00:22:37,856 --> 00:22:40,025
Twice in one day?
That's a bit much.

352
00:22:40,108 --> 00:22:41,193
Hey, what's that ringtone?

353
00:22:42,235 --> 00:22:44,696
A ringback tone? I had one?

354
00:22:46,031 --> 00:22:48,200
You don't even know
what your ringback tone is.

355
00:22:49,367 --> 00:22:51,244
Really?

356
00:22:51,328 --> 00:22:52,662
So I did have a ringback tone.

357
00:22:53,830 --> 00:22:54,664
Wait a second.

358
00:22:55,624 --> 00:22:56,833
Hey, then have I...

359
00:22:56,917 --> 00:22:59,628
Been paying for it every month
this whole time?

360
00:23:00,504 --> 00:23:01,379
Damn it.

361
00:23:01,463 --> 00:23:03,757
You used to pirate songs by Deux,

362
00:23:03,840 --> 00:23:05,217
so this is how you pay them back, asshole.

363
00:23:05,300 --> 00:23:06,927
Damn.

364
00:23:07,010 --> 00:23:08,970
Hey, was my ringback tone Deux?

365
00:23:09,805 --> 00:23:12,766
You aren't still dancing to Deux by
yourself at the park exercise spot, are you?

366
00:23:12,849 --> 00:23:16,603
Hey, Deux needs two
people to be Deux, man.

367
00:23:22,651 --> 00:23:25,612
What is it? Did you call because I didn't
send you the link for that omega-3?

368
00:23:30,867 --> 00:23:31,952
Hey, Geobang, where are you?

369
00:23:33,286 --> 00:23:34,371
I'm home.

370
00:23:37,541 --> 00:23:39,876
Come out. Let's have a quick drink
for two hours, then head home.

371
00:23:43,547 --> 00:23:44,923
Sure, okay.

372
00:23:58,979 --> 00:24:00,147
You really are a regular.

373
00:24:01,189 --> 00:24:02,023
Right?

374
00:24:03,817 --> 00:24:05,527
I only suggested you get in touch.

375
00:24:06,528 --> 00:24:09,072
I didn't think you'd go see him
right away, today.

376
00:24:10,282 --> 00:24:11,491
If you keep putting it off,

377
00:24:11,575 --> 00:24:13,493
you might end up seeing one another
at a funeral.

378
00:24:18,498 --> 00:24:19,332
Pour me one.

379
00:24:20,792 --> 00:24:22,460
Hey, didn't you live in Sillim?

380
00:24:22,544 --> 00:24:24,087
That was eight years ago, man.

381
00:24:24,171 --> 00:24:25,172
Do you still live in Yeonsinnae?

382
00:24:25,255 --> 00:24:27,340
That was when I was newly
married, dumbass.

383
00:24:27,424 --> 00:24:28,884
So where do you live now?

384
00:24:28,967 --> 00:24:30,552
Anyang.

385
00:24:31,761 --> 00:24:33,138
- Anyang?
- Yeah.

386
00:24:33,889 --> 00:24:35,307
You're a real piece of work.

387
00:24:36,349 --> 00:24:39,186
Hey, I live in Anyang now.

388
00:24:39,811 --> 00:24:40,812
Oh, yeah?

389
00:24:40,896 --> 00:24:42,439
Yeah, man.

390
00:24:45,942 --> 00:24:47,903
Then why'd we meet in Seoul?

391
00:24:47,986 --> 00:24:48,820
Good point.

392
00:24:48,904 --> 00:24:50,238
Damn.

393
00:24:50,322 --> 00:24:52,324
Ah, screw it.

394
00:24:52,407 --> 00:24:53,742
When did you move to Anyang?

395
00:24:53,825 --> 00:24:55,994
Hey, I officially moved to Anyang...

396
00:24:56,077 --> 00:24:57,662
- I moved in today.
- Today?

397
00:24:57,746 --> 00:24:58,997
Yeah.

398
00:24:59,080 --> 00:24:59,956
Look at this guy.

399
00:25:00,040 --> 00:25:01,708
You're a funny one, aren't you?

400
00:25:01,791 --> 00:25:04,336
You moved to Anyang without even
letting your big brother know?

401
00:25:04,419 --> 00:25:07,547
Well, since you're the
senior Anyang resident...

402
00:25:07,631 --> 00:25:08,465
You can pay for the drinks tonight.

403
00:25:15,972 --> 00:25:19,100
♪ Who am I, and where am I? ♪

404
00:25:19,184 --> 00:25:23,772
♪ Someone's calling me
from far away ♪

405
00:25:23,855 --> 00:25:27,651
♪ Who am I, and where am I? ♪

406
00:25:27,734 --> 00:25:32,113
♪ From now on, we'll only
move forward ♪

407
00:25:32,197 --> 00:25:35,742
♪ No matter how much I look around ♪

408
00:25:35,825 --> 00:25:39,704
♪ There was always nothing
but darkness by my side ♪

409
00:25:40,455 --> 00:25:42,749
♪ The only thing I could feel ♪

410
00:25:42,832 --> 00:25:48,421
♪ Was the sound of my labored,
